@startuml Sequence Diagram - Certificate Flow
!theme plain
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing true
skinparam roundCorner 15
skinparam defaultFontName "Segoe UI"
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam sequence {
    ArrowColor #34495E
    LifeLineBorderColor #7F8C8D
    ParticipantBackgroundColor #2C3E50
    ParticipantFontColor #FFFFFF
    ParticipantBorderColor #2C3E50
}
skinparam note {
    BackgroundColor #FFFDE7
    BorderColor #F9A825
    FontSize 11
}

title <size:22><b>Academic Event Management System</b></size>\n<size:16><color:#666666>Sequence Diagram — Certificate Generation & Download</color></size>\n
footer <size:10>Prepared for Black Book Submission | Academic Event Management System</size>

actor "<b>Admin</b>" as Admin
actor "<b>Student</b>" as Student
participant "<b>React Frontend</b>\n(AdminCertificates)" as FE_Admin
participant "<b>React Frontend</b>\n(StudentCertificates)" as FE_Student
participant "<b>CertificateController</b>\n(/api/certificates)" as CC
participant "<b>CertificateService</b>" as CS
participant "<b>CertificatePdfService</b>\n(iTextPDF 5.5.13)" as CPS
participant "<b>NotificationService</b>" as NS
participant "<b>EmailService</b>\n(@Async)" as ES
database "<b>PostgreSQL</b>" as DB

== Phase 1: Admin Generates Certificate ==

Admin -> FE_Admin : Click "Generate Certificate"\nfor Student #5 in Event #3
activate FE_Admin
FE_Admin -> CC : **POST** /api/certificates/generate/12\n(registrationId = 12)
activate CC
CC -> CS : generateCertificate(registrationId)
activate CS

CS -> DB : findByRegistrationId(12)
activate DB
DB --> CS : Optional.empty() — \n<b>No existing certificate</b>
deactivate DB

CS -> DB : findById(12) — load Registration
activate DB
DB --> CS : Registration\n(status=Approved, attendance=Present)
deactivate DB

CS -> CS : Validate eligibility:\n✓ Status = Approved\n✓ Attendance = Present

CS -> CS : Generate certificateNumber\n"CERT-" + timestamp

CS -> DB : save(Certificate)\nissueDate=today, status="Generated"
activate DB
DB --> CS : Saved Certificate\n(id = 7, number = "CERT-1725...")
deactivate DB

CS -> NS : createNotification(student,\n"Certificate Generated",\n"CERTIFICATE")
activate NS
NS -> DB : save(Notification)\nstatus = UNREAD
activate DB
DB --> NS : Saved
deactivate DB
deactivate NS

CS -> ES : sendCertificateNotification(\nstudent, certificateNumber)\n<b>@Async</b>
activate ES
ES --> CS : (email queued)
deactivate ES

CS --> CC : Certificate object\n(id=7, number="CERT-1725...")
deactivate CS
CC --> FE_Admin : **200 OK**
deactivate CC
FE_Admin --> Admin : "Certificate Generated!" ✅
deactivate FE_Admin

== Phase 2: Student Downloads Certificate ==

Student -> FE_Student : Click "Download Certificate"\nfor Event #3
activate FE_Student
FE_Student -> CC : **GET** /api/certificates/download/12
activate CC

CC -> CS : getByRegistration(12)
activate CS
CS -> DB : findByRegistrationId(12)
activate DB
DB --> CS : Certificate object
deactivate DB
CS --> CC : Certificate
deactivate CS

CC -> CPS : generateCertificate(certificate)
activate CPS

note over CPS
  <b>CertificatePdfService</b> — PDF Generation Pipeline:
  1. Determine event category (Workshop/Technical/Seminar/Cultural/Hackathon)
  2. Load corresponding background PNG (2480×3508px)
  3. Process college logo (remove white background → transparent)
  4. Overlay text elements with proper fonts
  5. Add handwritten signature image
end note

CPS -> CPS : <b>Step 1:</b> Determine event category\nfrom Event → EventCategory

CPS -> CPS : <b>Step 2:</b> Load background PNG\n`certificate/bg_workshop.png`\n(or bg_technical, bg_seminar, etc.)

CPS -> CPS : <b>Step 3:</b> Load college logo\n`certificate/college_logo.png`\nRemove white background (transparent)

CPS -> CPS : <b>Step 4:</b> Draw text elements:\n• "Certificate of Completion" (title)\n• "This is to certify that" (italic)\n• Student full name (large, bold)\n• Event title\n• Event date\n• Issue date

CPS -> CPS : <b>Step 5:</b> Draw handwritten signature\nimage at bottom-right

CPS --> CC : byte[] (PDF binary data)
deactivate CPS

CC --> FE_Student : **200 OK**\n`Content-Type: application/pdf`\n`Content-Disposition: attachment`
deactivate CC

FE_Student -> FE_Student : Trigger browser download\nfilename: "CERT-1725...pdf"

FE_Student --> Student : PDF file downloaded ✅
deactivate FE_Student

note over Admin, DB
  <b>Certificate Generation Summary:</b>
  • Admin triggers generation → validates eligibility (Approved + Present)
  • Certificate number: "CERT-{timestamp}" (unique)
  • PDF generated with iTextPDF 5.5.13.3
  • Category-specific backgrounds: Workshop, Technical, Seminar, Cultural, Hackathon
  • College logo with transparent background overlay
  • Dynamic text: student name, event name, date, signature
  • Notification + email sent to student asynchronously
end note

@enduml
